dxgi: Say how long the game's frames take, in the log.

Whether a game stutters could only be seen by someone playing it, or by a recorder beside it
that takes processor time from the game and made Call of Duty: WWII stutter by itself. The swap
chain now counts the time from one Present to the next (a clock read and a count per frame, in
steps of half a millisecond up to 200 ms) and says in the log every half minute, and when it
goes, how the frames of the whole run so far were:

  DXGI: frame times: 54000 frames in 900 s, median 16.5 ms, 95% 17.0 ms, 99% 33.5 ms,
  worst 412.0 ms, 31 over 50 ms

"macos/steamplay record" keeps the last such line with the run. The time a window is hidden
(Present says it is occluded) is no frame's. Direct3D 10 and 11 only: Direct3D 9, 12 and Vulkan
do not come through here.

LOCAL TO THIS PORT, NOT FOR DXMT. Applied by macos/build-dxmt.sh to
github.com/athei/dxmt at 01e59e9bde030f105937f249afaac92ada01b4d7, after 0001 to 0009.
Written with an AI assistant (Claude). DXMT does not accept contributions made or
co-authored by AI (its CONTRIBUTING.md), so this patch must not be sent to it as a pull
request.
